         check found the arm's true max reach is ~0.499 m (joint-limited, measured,
         less than the naive fully-outstretched estimate of 0.530 m), and x=0.45
         put targets at ~0.56 m from the shoulder: physically outside the arm's
         workspace, confirmed by the IK solver saturating exactly at max reach
         along the line to the target. x=0.28 puts all three ~0.43-0.44 m out,
         with margin under 0.499 m. Re-run verify_arm_ik.py if bricks move again.
         brick2's y moved from 0 (dead center) to -0.07: at y=0, reaching it
         required the right (or left) shoulder to rotate across the body's own
         centerline, producing a real torso/shoulder self-collision for BOTH
         arms and leaving the physically-simulated gripper site ~4.4cm off
         target (vs a 2cm tolerance) even though the IK solve itself converged
         fine -- confirmed the pregrasp height wasn't the cause (self-collision
         persisted up to 20cm above the brick) and that only a lateral shift
         resolved it. At y=-0.07 the right arm reaches it with the self-collision
         gone and ~1.6cm error. See CLAUDE.md's "Arm IK" section.
